  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Rama Setu, also known as Adam''s Bridge, is a chain of natural limestone
    shoals between Pamban Island (Rameswaram Island) in India and Mannar Island in
    Sri Lanka, believed in Hindu mythology to be a bridge built by Rama''s army to
    reach Lanka.  It is believed to have been formed between 7,000 and 18,000 years
    ago. The length of the limestone bridge is 48 km. '
