  m_text: Brihadishvara Temple, called Rajarajesvaram and known locally as Thanjai
    Periya Kovil and Peruvudaiyar Kovil, is a Shaivite Hindu temple built in a Chola
    architectural style located on the south bank of the Cauvery river in Thanjavur,
    Tamil Nadu. It is one of the largest Hindu temples. It is also called Dakshina
    Meru built by Chola emperor Rajaraja I between 1003 and 1010 CE, the temple is
    a part of the UNESCO World Heritage Site known as the "Great Living Chola Temples"
