  m_text: "The Masjid-i-Jehan-Numa, commonly known as the Jama Masjid of Delhi, is
    one of the largest Sunni mosques in India.\r\n\tIts builder is the Mughal emperor
    Shah Jahan, between 1644 and 1656, and inaugurated by its first Imam, Syed Abdul
    Ghafoor Shah Bukhari. Situated in the Mughal capital of Shahjahanabad (today
    Old Delhi), it served as the imperial mosque of the Mughal emperors until the
    demise of the empire in 1857."
