  m_text: 'The Luxor Temple is a large Ancient Egyptian temple complex located on
    the east bank of the Nile River in the city today known as Luxor (ancient Thebes)
    and was constructed approximately 1400 BCE. In the Egyptian language it was known
    as ipet resyt, "the southern sanctuary". It was one of the two primary temples
    on the east bank, the other being Karnak. Unlike the other temples in Thebes,
    Luxor temple is not dedicated to a cult god or a deified version of the pharaoh
    in death. Instead, Luxor temple is dedicated to the rejuvenation of kingship;
    it may have been where many of the pharaohs of Egypt were crowned in reality
    or conceptually '
