      m_Calls: []
  m_text: The Kailasa Temple in Ellora, Maharashtra, is a massive rock-cut temple
    dedicated to Lord Shiva, carved from a single basalt rock in the 8th century
    by the Rashtrakuta king Krishna I. It is an architectural marvel, featuring intricate
    sculptures, massive pillars, and detailed relief work inspired by Mount Kailash.
    This UNESCO-listed masterpiece is one of the largest monolithic structures in
    the world.
